    LLM: 'Identify four cards of the same rank close together near the end of the layout; move these sweeper cards as a group toward the front without covering them until the end.\n\nPrefer 3-left moves when they do not block future sweeper sequences. Preserve connector piles that enable multiple 3-left paths.\n\nTreat the row as a dependency graph. Odds of winning are around one in a hundred. Alfred Sheinwold suggests considering five piles or fewer a win.',
